<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · river</p><h1 class="enc-title">Arade</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Arade is a river of the western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/algarve">Algarve</a> in southern Portugal, flowing past <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/silves">Silves</a> to the Atlantic at Portimão. In Roman and Islamic times it was navigable up to Silves, which made the town a river port and the chief city of the Algarve. Later silting reduced navigation, and its estuary now forms the harbour of Portimão.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/arade.jpg" alt="Arade" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Patrícia Nunes · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Ponte_Ferrovi%C3%A1ria_de_Portim%C3%A3o.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
